  "topic": "Processor Pipelining and Data Forwarding",
  "explanation": "Processor pipelining improves instruction execution speed by overlapping the execution stages of multiple instructions.  However, data hazards can occur when an instruction depends on the result of a previous instruction that hasn't completed yet. Data forwarding is a technique to mitigate these hazards by bypassing the result directly from a later pipeline stage to an earlier one, preventing stalls and maintaining pipeline efficiency.",
  "syntax": "Data forwarding is implemented within the processor's control logic and is not directly expressed in assembly code.  It's a hardware mechanism that dynamically detects and resolves data hazards during pipeline execution.",
